.TH PKIT-HELP 1 "April 2026" "pkit 0.1.2" "General Commands Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBpkit-help\fR \- Display help for pkit or a named subcommand.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkit help [\fITOPIC\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Display usage information for the main \f[CR]pkit\f[R] command or for a specific subcommand.
.PP
When invoked without arguments, \f[CR]help\f[R] shows the top\-level command overview.
.PP
When a subcommand name is supplied, help for that command is displayed.
.PP
This command is functionally equivalent to invoking \f[CR]\-\-help\f[R], but provides a consistent entry point for scripted or explicit help access.

.SH OPTIONS


.SH EXAMPLES
Examples:
.IP
.EX
Show top\-level help:
    pkit help

Show help for a specific subcommand:
    pkit help add

Equivalent using the standard flag:
    pkit add \-\-help
.EE

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkit (1)

